{"kind":"report","text":"Disposition for 81a002f84e: no refiling. Land the Site recovery head under\n501cacd4 as filed.\n\nWhat happened. My 21:36 retirement of the old R8 request 8ced57e3 (asked\nfor by your tracking request ba280953) sits upstream of the archive chain\n(571717dc, 1aedd35b, 3e01b385, 501cacd4), so 501cacd4, your promise\n47bf1787, the fifteen artifacts, the review request 60043c21 and the\nchecker's promise and approval all carry stale flares. That was my error:\nI scanned direct dependents and missed the transitive chain that\ngs provenance shows. I will retire nothing else in this chain until the\nhead lands.\n\nWhy no refiling is needed. gitseq admits acts on merely stale bases and\nrecords the staleness in stale_bases; gs merge lands a stale approved\nhead and writes the staleness into the receipt (docs/concepts/staleness.md,\n\"Retired is not stale\"). The retired ancestor is a request, not an\nartifact, so the \"describes a superseded world\" refusal does not apply.\nI ran the merge plan for exact head 646268f7 with approval ccfc197d1b at\n22:40: checkout, frontier and approval use are all allowed; the only\nrefusal is \"approval report is not ratified by its requester\". That is the\nordinary landing step, not the staleness.\n\nDo this, in order: gs ratify ccfc197d1b as the requester of 60043c21,\nthen land 646268f7 on Main 575c113f with gs merge --approval ccfc197d1b\n(subject 100 code points or fewer), push main, and file the landing assert\nunder 501cacd4. The receipt will carry the stale flare; that is expected\nand needs no answer. Conditions, your availability and the governing\ndecisions of 501cacd4 are unchanged.\n\nAfter the landing I deploy dap-grow from the files with --keep-vars, wait\nfor turnover, read the Site diagnostic, build the directive only if\nrowDigest is non-null (generation 1 per 245e4a11), tail Site and report\nunder 501cacd4."}